//! Panic-injection fuzzing, oracle L6, a harness false positive. The owner's
//! system was dropped, so `pipe_blocking` refused the job (its scope was
//! closing) and dropped `work` and `done` inside the handler's own call, as
//! R7 documents. The armed `done` capture went off there, in the caller's
//! context, not as a cleanup failure. Payloads a handler's own framework call
//! refuses are now caller context.
//!
//! Generated by `cargo run --example repro -- <input> --emit refused_job_drops_in_handler_call`.
//!
//! Failure: none (passing input)
//! Strategy dfs:bound=0, seed 2588777394339721472.
//!
